    "sections": {
        "description": "<p>WordPress Block to display post type name on a website. Can be used in templates like search results. Build for the block/site editor.</p>\n<h3>Road map</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Add optional prefix and suffix</li>\n<li>Add option to change the tag from p to other tags</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>Repos</h3>\n<p>WP.org Plugin plugin repo aka. block directory: (submitted)<br />\nSource on GitHub: https://github.com/CrossMediaCloud/Post-Type-Name/</p>\n",
        "installation": "<ol>\n<li>Upload the plugin files to the <code>/wp-content/plugins/post-type-name</code> directory, or install the plugin through the WordPress plugins screen directly.</li>\n<li>Activate the plugin through the &#8216;Plugins&#8217; screen in WordPress</li>\n</ol>\n",
        "changelog": "<h4>1.0.1 (06.01.2025)</h4>\n<ul>\n<li>Update SVN to release plugin</li>\n</ul>\n<h4>1.0.0 (26.09.2024)</h4>\n<ul>\n<li>First release to WP.org</li>\n</ul>\n<h4>0.1.0</h4>\n<ul>\n<li>Kick ofg the block</li>\n</ul>\n"
    },
